in my 2026-2030 buildout column.\",\"signpost\":\"The G7 GDP-weighted 10y sovereign real yield (10y nominal minus 10y inflation swap) averages below 1.00% for twelve consecutive months, with the 10y JGB real yield still below 0.50%.\"} | {\"by_when\":\"Jun 30, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Removes the physical-energization cap that holds my CQ3 P90 at 2.9 and that makes power/grid (+7.5) and construction/trades (+6.5) my two best 2026-2030 rows. CQ3 P90 rises to ~3.2 and P50 to ~2.0; CQ6-A rises from 18 to ~24 with B falling. My upward correction to AI-Q4 (toward 0.73) reverses toward the locked 0.66, and realized AI-Q3 load returns toward the locked 998 TWh P50. In the matrix, power/grid buildout falls from 7.5 to ~4.5 and construction from 6.5 to ~4.0 as the scarcity rent evaporates, while the AI-complex column rises ~3 pp in A and B.\",\"signpost\":\"Generator step-up transformer lead times fall back below 80 weeks AND gas turbine lead times below 36 months, on OEM order-book disclosures or NERC/EIA reporting — against >160 weeks and five years respectively as of Q1 2026.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'growth'."}}